                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Chaos Theory runs amazingly on the Steam Deck! After applying the FusionFix widescreen fix, the game not only supports widescreen properly but also gets its controls fixed. You can even change the night vision goggles color and make the back torso LCD behave just like it does in Blacklist.\n\nThe game surprisingly looks modern on the Steam Deck OLED with just a few tweaks to brightness and contrast. It’s a shame I haven’t found a way to enable native HDR, though.\n\nPerformance and battery life are excellent, too. I’m getting around 4–5 hours of battery life at 60 Hz with a TDP of just 5–7 W.\n\nOverall, this has turned out to be one of my best gaming experiences on the Steam Deck. It’s amazing how well this classic holds up with a few tweaks, delivering a fantastic experience on a handheld.",
